<dc:title>Zebulon Pike to Thomas Jefferson, October 29, 1807</dc:title>
<dc:description>Among the items Captain Zebulon Pike sent to President Thomas Jefferson from the western United States was a pair of grizzly bear cubs. Jefferson kept them in a garden on the south side of the &lt;a href=&quot;http://mallhistory.org/items/show/66&quot;&gt;White House&lt;/a&gt; for a short time before sending the animals to a museum in Philadelphia.</dc:description>
